From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate 0402-black-world-03-upscale-trace-per-program.patch

Source: 0402-black-world-03-upscale-trace-per-program.patch
network's handle inventory

T21 (runs 78, 79): EDEN_NX2_UPSCALE_TRACE's one cap of 256 lines was used up at 35-39 s by the ten
movie programs, because the text carried the cbuf0 address, which changes every dispatch. Not one
line was left for the gameplay program (first HMMA at 0xc00), whose outcomes were the point.
Likewise EDEN_NX2_SAMPLE_AT (20th blit) and EDEN_NX2_TRACE_AFTER_UPSCALE (30th blit) count all
programs together, so the movies' blits spent them before gameplay.

- The trace text no longer names the cbuf0 address, and each program gets up to 24 lines of its
  own.
- A program's first paired outcome also lists its handle inventory: every texture handle the
  program reads and every surface it stores to, with address, size and format ("; handles:
  r@0xc0 tic 1234 0x8114001000 2560x1440 format 32 ... w@0xd0 ..."). That names what the
  network reads besides the drawn frame (a history, a 1920x1080 image, motion vectors) and so
  which image run75's one-time plain copy can have shown.
- The 20th-blit sampling and the 30th-blit draw trace (40 draws after the upscale, with their
  render targets and sampled handles: what the game reads after the network) count per program.

Behaviour without the switches is unchanged. Clang syntax check, no warnings, on the T20 tree
with black-world-01 and 02. Not built, not run.

